{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119444","id":3679050547,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7bSdsz","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119444","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119444.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119444.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119444","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119444/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119444/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119444/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ad4a7ee52ad28b993dfe51f13c1c780b3dc222fa","number":119444,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Implement get_latency method for coreaudio on MacOS","user":{"login":"mattbearman","id":717345,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNzM0NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/717345?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman","html_url":"https://github.com/mattbearman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattbearman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nCurrently calling `AudioServer.get_output_latency()` on a Mac will always return `0`, as the `get_latency()` function is not defined in the CoreAudio driver, so it falls back to the virtual function in `audio_server.h`, which just returns `0`\r\n\r\nThis PR adds the `get_latency()` function in CoreAudio (for Mac only, other devices using CoreAudio, such as iOS, will still report 0 - I'll tackle that in a future PR)\r\n\r\nI've tested this on a 2023 M3 MacBook Pro running MacOS 15, and a 2017 Intel MacBook Pro running MacOS 13, with a few different audio devices on each (built in speakers, headphones, USB interfaces), and the latency reported appeared correct in all instances\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe basis for the latency calculations came from this discussion on the [JUCE framework forum](https://forum.juce.com/t/macos-round-trip-latency/45278), as well as the CoreAudio docs and my own experimentation\r\n\r\nRegarding stream latency, in an ideal world when there are multiple streams we'd figure out which stream was currently being used, however I couldn't find a reliable way to do that. The approach here of using the maximum reported stream latency seems like a safe compromise, especially considering every single external audio device I tested reported a stream latency of zero anyway\r\n\r\nIn my testing only the built in audio devices actually report a stream latency, and they only ever have the one stream 🤷\r\n\r\n## AI disclosure\r\n\r\nI didn't use any AI in the development of this","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097780,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc3ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:macos","name":"platform:macos","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"arc